# LF everywhere in the repository, checked out as LF on every platform.
#
# Why this exists: 31 tracked files were LF in HEAD but CRLF in the working tree, so
# editing any of them produced a diff touching every line. That happened for real —
# a 26-line change to the lesson player showed up as 932 changed lines, which makes a
# review impossible without altering any behaviour. Zero files were CRLF in HEAD, so
# LF was already the convention; nothing was enforcing it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets git must not touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
